###################################################################################
## HDL Shared FIFO CDC Constraints
##
## Auto-generated by gen_constraints.py
##
## !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
## !! REQUIREMENT -- these constraints are ONLY valid if, for every FIFO:
## !!   * the clock on the FIFO ViClk  port is 80 MHz (target BusClk / PllClk80)
## !!   * the clock on the FIFO BusClk port is 250 MHz (DmaClk)
## !! The periods below are hard-coded.  With any other ViClk frequency these
## !! constraints are silently wrong -- Vivado reports nothing, and a faster
## !! ViClk leaves the clock-domain crossings under-constrained.
## !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
##
## Each constraint explicitly targets specific synchronizer flip-flops inside
## each CDC component instance.  If the design changes, only the known safe
## flip-flops are relaxed -- new logic will NOT be silently caught.
##
## Clock domains (effective periods from the target clock definitions).
## NOTE: the FIFO port names do not match the target clock names --
## the FIFO BusClk port is driven by DmaClk, NOT by the target's BusClk.
##
##   Variable        FIFO port  Driven by (UserHdl)        Freq       Effective period
##   hdl_dmaclk_T    BusClk     DmaClk                     250 MHz    3.7496000400 ns
##   hdl_userclk_T   ViClk      target BusClk (PllClk80)    80 MHz    12.2487501250 ns
##   Formula: 1/(freq*(1+PPM/1e6)) - jitter  [PPM=100, jitter=250ps]
##
## Section comments say "user" for the ViClk-port side and "DMA" for the
## BusClk-port side.
##
## Writer FIFOs (TargetToHost): NiSharedFifoWriterCorex
## Reader FIFOs (HostToTarget): NiSharedFifoReaderCorex
##
###################################################################################

set hdl_dmaclk_T 3.7496000400
set hdl_userclk_T 12.2487501250

